The original explicit branch in [#2285](https://github.com/EnzymeAD/Enzyme.jl/issues/2285) also reproduces in the LLVM backend without Julia. Clang 21.1.8 at `-O1 -ffp-contract=off` lowers the conditional to a multiply followed by a select. In reverse mode the discarded product receives a zero adjoint. Multiplying that zero by an infinite operand makes the derivative NaN.

```c
#include <math.h>
#include <stdio.h>

extern double __enzyme_autodiff(void *, ...);
extern int enzyme_const;

double f(double a, double x) {
    if (!isinf(a))
        x += a * x;
    return x;
}

int main(void) {
    double dx = __enzyme_autodiff((void *)f, enzyme_const, (double)INFINITY, 1.0);
    printf("value=%g dx=%g\n", f(INFINITY, 1.0), dx);
}
```

With the LLVM 21 Enzyme plugin in `$PLUGIN`, run

```sh
clang-21 -O1 -fno-inline -ffp-contract=off -S -emit-llvm example.c -o example.ll
opt-21 -load-pass-plugin="$PLUGIN" -passes=enzyme -S example.ll -o derivative.ll
lli-21 derivative.ll
```

At either infinity, the function returns its input `x`, so its derivative in `x` should be 1. Upstream `0231d1a7` gives NaN. The repaired build `0eb02b67` gives 1. Both give 3 when `a=2`. For the related branch `if (x >= 0 && x <= 1) return x*x; return -INFINITY;`, the repair gives a zero derivative at NaN and either infinity and retains a derivative of 1 at 0.5. Disabling select protection in the same repaired build reproduces both failures. The unguarded square still gives a NaN derivative at NaN.

The first change identifies floating-point instructions whose differential contributions are masked by a select. The second protects masked products, whose partials can be nonfinite even without division. This approach also affects eager selects that produce the same LLVM IR. The two original patches apply in order to upstream `0fa6f840`, using `git apply -C1` for the first patch. The numerical comparison used the integrated repaired build. [Select analysis](https://github.com/nsiccha/Enzyme/commit/0a3566d873e9f4054e5dfc4e47fd48c22391a65d) · [Masked products](https://github.com/nsiccha/Enzyme/commit/cad5bf297b84d58639e2fbdaa0e4724936343bb1)
